{
 "n": 3,
 "title": "From huddle to whistle: how one play works",
 "html": "<p><strong>Downs:</strong> the offense gets four tries (\"downs\") to gain 10 yards. Gain them and the count resets to \"1st and 10.\" Fall short and the other team gets the ball, so on 4th down most teams punt or kick a field goal instead. \"3rd and 4\" means third try, 4 yards still to go.</p>\n<div class=\"diagram\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 214\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"How downs work: starting at the 25, a 4-yard gain makes it 2nd and 6, then a 7-yard gain earns a new first down and moves the line 10 yards\"><defs><marker id=\"m6w\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/></marker><marker id=\"m6y\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"20.0\" x2=\"20.0\" y1=\"20\" y2=\"176\" stroke=\"rgba(255,255,255,0.45)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"20.0\" y=\"192\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">20</text><line x1=\"65.0\" x2=\"65.0\" y1=\"20\" y2=\"176\" stroke=\"rgba(255,255,255,0.18)\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"110.0\" x2=\"110.0\" y1=\"20\" y2=\"176\" stroke=\"rgba(255,255,255,0.45)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"110.0\" y=\"192\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">30</text><line x1=\"155.0\" x2=\"155.0\" y1=\"20\" y2=\"176\" stroke=\"rgba(255,255,255,0.18)\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"200.0\" x2=\"200.0\" y1=\"20\" y2=\"176\" stroke=\"rgba(255,255,255,0.45)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"192\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">40</text><line x1=\"245.0\" x2=\"245.0\" y1=\"20\" y2=\"176\" stroke=\"rgba(255,255,255,0.18)\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"290.0\" x2=\"290.0\" y1=\"20\" y2=\"176\" stroke=\"rgba(255,255,255,0.45)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"290.0\" y=\"192\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">50</text><line x1=\"335.0\" x2=\"335.0\" y1=\"20\" y2=\"176\" stroke=\"rgba(255,255,255,0.18)\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"380.0\" x2=\"380.0\" y1=\"20\" y2=\"176\" stroke=\"rgba(255,255,255,0.45)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"380.0\" y=\"192\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">60</text><line x1=\"155.0\" x2=\"155.0\" y1=\"26\" y2=\"62\" stroke=\"#F2B705\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"65.0\" cy=\"44\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"4.5\" fill=\"#8B5A2B\" stroke=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M73.0 44 L99.0 44\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" marker-end=\"url(#m6w)\"/><text x=\"69.0\" y=\"33\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">1st & 10: gain 4</text><line x1=\"155.0\" x2=\"155.0\" y1=\"76\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#F2B705\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"101.0\" cy=\"94\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"4.5\" fill=\"#8B5A2B\" stroke=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M109.0 94 L162.0 94\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" marker-end=\"url(#m6w)\"/><text x=\"105.0\" y=\"83\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">2nd & 6: gain 7, passes the line</text><line x1=\"254.0\" x2=\"254.0\" y1=\"126\" y2=\"162\" stroke=\"#F2B705\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"164.0\" cy=\"144\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"4.5\" fill=\"#8B5A2B\" stroke=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"168.0\" y=\"133\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">New 1st & 10: the line moves 10 yards</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"208\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">Yellow = first-down line. Own 20 to own 60 shown.</text></svg></div><p class=\"note\">The yellow line is the first-down marker you see on TV. Reach it and you get a fresh set of four downs.</p>\n<p><strong>Before the snap:</strong> each team gets its call from the sideline, lines up, and the offense may move players around (a \"shift\" or \"motion\") to see how the defense reacts. The QB can change the play at the line (an \"audible\").</p>\n<h3>A pass play is a race against the clock</h3>\n<p>From the snap, the QB has only a few seconds before pass rushers reach him. Short routes are open in about 1.5 seconds; deep routes need 2.5 seconds or more because the receiver has to run 20+ yards first. The measure that shows who's winning the race is <strong>time to throw</strong>: seconds from snap to release.</p>\n<div class=\"diagram\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 160\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Timeline of a pass play: short throws happen in the first 1.5 seconds, mid routes around 2 seconds, deep routes after 2.5 seconds. Love averaged 2.26 seconds.\"><defs><marker id=\"m7w\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/></marker><marker id=\"m7y\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"62\" width=\"135.0\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.45)\"/><rect x=\"155.0\" y=\"62\" width=\"90.0\" height=\"24\" fill=\"rgba(242,183,5,.45)\"/><rect x=\"245.0\" y=\"62\" width=\"135.0\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"rgba(242,183,5,.95)\"/><text x=\"20.0\" y=\"104\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">0s</text><text x=\"110.0\" y=\"104\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">1s</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"104\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">2s</text><text x=\"290.0\" y=\"104\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">3s</text><text x=\"380.0\" y=\"104\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">4s</text><text x=\"87.5\" y=\"54\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">short throws</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"54\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">mid routes open</text><text x=\"312.5\" y=\"54\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#F2B705\">deep routes open</text><line x1=\"223.39999999999998\" x2=\"223.39999999999998\" y1=\"28\" y2=\"92\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"/><text x=\"223.39999999999998\" y=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">Love's average throw Thursday: 2.26 s</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"132\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">Atlanta hit him 12 times on 53 pass plays,</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"148\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">so he threw before the deep routes had time to open.</text></svg></div>\n<p><strong>Reading the diagram:</strong> on Thursday, Atlanta's rushers hit Jordan Love 12 times on 53 pass plays, about once every four or five throws. So he got rid of the ball fast, averaging 2.26 seconds, which is before most deep routes open. That's how pressure hurts an offense even without sacks: it forces short throws, and short throws rarely produce big plays.</p>\n<h3>Why running the ball \"kept Love off the field\"</h3>\n<p>Only one team's offense can be on the field at a time. And the <strong>game clock keeps running after a run</strong> (if the runner is tackled in bounds), while it <strong>stops after an incomplete pass</strong>. So a drive built on runs uses up more minutes.</p>\n<p>Atlanta ran the ball 41 times because its runs kept gaining yards. Each long, run-heavy drive burned several minutes. Every one of those minutes, Green Bay's offense, and its quarterback Love, sat on the bench. Fewer minutes with the ball means fewer drives, and fewer drives means fewer chances to score. Coaches call this \"controlling the clock,\" and it's also why run-heavy games tend to finish under the betting total.</p>\n<div class=\"diagram\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 188\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A run-heavy ten-play drive uses about six and a half minutes; a pass-heavy one with four incompletions uses about four\"><defs><marker id=\"m8w\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/></marker><marker id=\"m8y\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/></marker></defs><text x=\"20\" y=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">Same 10-play drive, two ways (illustration):</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"50\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">Run-heavy: clock keeps running between plays</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"58\" width=\"357.5\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"202.75\" y=\"73\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">about 6½ minutes</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"104\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">Pass-heavy with 4 incompletions: clock stops 4 times</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"112\" width=\"220.0\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.75)\"/><text x=\"130.0\" y=\"127\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">about 4 minutes</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"162\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">The extra 2½ minutes come off the other team’s time.</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"178\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">Their QB sits on the bench, gets fewer drives, scores less.</text></svg></div>\n<h3>Run plays: two ways to block</h3>\n<p><strong>Zone blocking:</strong> all five linemen step the same direction together and block whoever is in front of them. The RB watches where a gap opens and cuts into it. <strong>Gap blocking:</strong> the play is designed for one specific hole, and a lineman (often a guard) \"pulls,\" running behind the line to the other side to block a defender there.</p>\n<div class=\"diagram\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 196\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Inside zone: the line steps together and the running back aims at the middle, cutting into whichever gap opens\"><defs><marker id=\"m9w\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/></marker><marker id=\"m9y\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"0\" x2=\"400\" y1=\"100\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#F2B705\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"6\" y=\"95\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.75)\">line of scrimmage</text><path d=\"M150 102 L164 86\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#m9w)\"/><path d=\"M176 102 L190 86\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#m9w)\"/><path d=\"M202 102 L216 86\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#m9w)\"/><path d=\"M228 102 L242 86\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#m9w)\"/><path d=\"M254 102 L268 86\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#m9w)\"/><path d=\"M202 178 L224 122 L230 64\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" marker-end=\"url(#m9w)\"/><path d=\"M224 122 L182 60\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\" marker-end=\"url(#m9w)\"/><rect x=\"140.0\" y=\"104.0\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><rect x=\"166.0\" y=\"104.0\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><rect x=\"192.0\" y=\"104.0\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><rect x=\"218.0\" y=\"104.0\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><rect x=\"244.0\" y=\"104.0\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><circle cx=\"286\" cy=\"116\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"286\" y=\"119.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">TE</text><circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"114\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"117.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">WR</text><circle cx=\"96\" cy=\"120\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"96\" y=\"123.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">WR</text><circle cx=\"372\" cy=\"114\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"372\" y=\"117.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">WR</text><circle cx=\"202\" cy=\"136\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"202\" y=\"139.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">QB</text><circle cx=\"202\" cy=\"180\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"202\" y=\"183.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">RB</text><circle cx=\"163\" cy=\"76\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"163\" y=\"79.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">DL</text><circle cx=\"191\" cy=\"76\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"191\" y=\"79.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">DL</text><circle cx=\"219\" cy=\"76\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"219\" y=\"79.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">DL</text><circle cx=\"247\" cy=\"76\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"247\" y=\"79.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">DL</text><circle cx=\"185\" cy=\"42\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"185\" y=\"45.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">LB</text><circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"42\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"240\" y=\"45.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">LB</text><text x=\"296\" y=\"60\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">RB runs at the</text><text x=\"296\" y=\"73\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">middle, then cuts</text><text x=\"296\" y=\"86\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">into the open gap</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"18\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">All 5 linemen step the same way together</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">dashed = the cutback option</text></svg></div><p class=\"note\"><strong>Zone blocking</strong> (inside zone). White arrows are the linemen’s first steps and the RB’s path.</p><div class=\"diagram\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 196\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Power: the backside guard pulls across the formation to lead the running back through a planned hole\"><defs><marker id=\"m10w\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/></marker><marker id=\"m10y\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"0\" x2=\"400\" y1=\"100\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#F2B705\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"6\" y=\"95\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.75)\">line of scrimmage</text><path d=\"M202 102 L184 84\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#m10w)\"/><path d=\"M228 102 L210 84\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#m10w)\"/><path d=\"M254 102 L236 84\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#m10w)\"/><path d=\"M150 102 L140 88\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#m10w)\"/><path d=\"M176 126 L176 130 L262 130 L270 84\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#F2B705\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"1 0\" marker-end=\"url(#m10y)\"/><path d=\"M202 178 L262 144 L276 50\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" marker-end=\"url(#m10w)\"/><rect x=\"140.0\" y=\"104.0\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><rect x=\"166.0\" y=\"104.0\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><rect x=\"192.0\" y=\"104.0\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><rect x=\"218.0\" y=\"104.0\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><rect x=\"244.0\" y=\"104.0\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><circle cx=\"286\" cy=\"116\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"286\" y=\"119.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">TE</text><circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"114\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"117.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">WR</text><circle cx=\"96\" cy=\"120\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"96\" y=\"123.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">WR</text><circle cx=\"372\" cy=\"114\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"372\" y=\"117.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">WR</text><circle cx=\"202\" cy=\"136\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"202\" y=\"139.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">QB</text><circle cx=\"202\" cy=\"180\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"202\" y=\"183.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">RB</text><circle cx=\"163\" cy=\"76\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"163\" y=\"79.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">DL</text><circle cx=\"191\" cy=\"76\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"191\" y=\"79.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">DL</text><circle cx=\"219\" cy=\"76\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"219\" y=\"79.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">DL</text><circle cx=\"247\" cy=\"76\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"247\" y=\"79.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">DL</text><circle cx=\"185\" cy=\"42\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"185\" y=\"45.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">LB</text><circle cx=\"270\" cy=\"42\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"270\" y=\"45.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">LB</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"148\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#F2B705\">guard pulls</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"18\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">Gap run: the play is built for one hole.</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">The left guard (yellow path) runs behind the line</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"45\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">and leads the RB through it.</text></svg></div><p class=\"note\"><strong>Gap blocking</strong> (power). The pulling guard is the giveaway on TV: watch for a lineman running sideways behind the line.</p>\n<p><strong>The whistle:</strong> the play ends when the ball carrier is tackled or steps out of bounds, someone scores, or a pass hits the ground. The officials mark the spot and the next down begins.</p>\n<h3>How to read 3rd down</h3>\n<p>Look at the yellow first-down line on the TV screen. <strong>3rd and short</strong> (1–2 yards): expect a run, because a run gains 2 yards often. <strong>3rd and long</strong> (8+ yards): everyone knows it's a pass. The defense goes to <strong>dime</strong> (six DBs, Lesson 2) because it doesn't need run stoppers. And its pass rushers stop worrying about the run and sprint straight at the QB from the snap. Coaches call that \"pinning your ears back,\" like a dog flattening its ears to run full speed. That's why 3rd and long is so hard to convert.</p>\n<div class=\"diagram\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 262\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Third and one: heavy offense against a base defense with eight in the box\"><defs><marker id=\"m11w\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/></marker><marker id=\"m11y\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"106\" y=\"84\" width=\"214\" height=\"62\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"rgba(242,183,5,.10)\" stroke=\"#F2B705\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><line x1=\"0\" x2=\"400\" y1=\"150\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#F2B705\" stroke-width=\"